@@ -0,0 +1,44 @@
+Feature: Todo persistence
+  As a user
+  I want my todos to be saved across page reloads
+  So that I do not lose my task list
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded
+
+  Rule: Save todos to localStorage
+
+  Scenario: Persist todos after creating them
+    Given I type "Buy milk" into the new-todo input and press Enter
+    And I type "Walk the dog" into the new-todo input and press Enter
+    When the app is reloaded
+    Then the todo list shows 2 items
+    And the todo list shows "Buy milk"
+    And the todo list shows "Walk the dog"
+
+  Scenario: Persist completion state
+    Given I type "Buy milk" into the new-todo input and press Enter
+    And I click the toggle checkbox on "Buy milk"
+    When the app is reloaded
+    Then "Buy milk" has the class "completed"
+
+  Scenario: Persist todos after editing
+    Given I type "Buy milk" into the new-todo input and press Enter
+    When I double-click the label of "Buy milk"
+    And I clear the edit input and type "Buy organic milk" and press Enter in the edit input
+    When the app is reloaded
+    Then the todo list shows "Buy organic milk"
+
+  Scenario: Persist active filter on reload
+    Given I type "Buy milk" into the new-todo input and press Enter
+    And I navigate to the "#/active" route
+    When the app is reloaded
+    Then the "Active" filter link has the "selected" class
+
+  Rule: Editing mode must not be persisted
+
+  Scenario: Editing mode is not persisted
+    Given I type "Buy milk" into the new-todo input and press Enter
+    And I double-click the label of "Buy milk"
+    When the app is reloaded
+    Then no todo item has the "editing" class
\ No newline at end of file
