@@ -0,0 +1,47 @@
+Feature: Todo routing
+  As a user
+  I want to filter the todo list by completion state
+  So that I can focus on active or completed tasks
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded
+    And I create the following todos:
+      | Buy milk    |
+      | Walk the dog |
+      | Write code  |
+    And I click the toggle checkbox on "Walk the dog"
+
+  Rule: Default route shows all todos
+
+  Scenario: Default route shows all todos
+    Given the URL hash is "#/"
+    Then the todo list shows 3 items
+    And the "All" filter link has the "selected" class
+
+  Rule: Active filter
+
+  Scenario: Active filter shows only active todos
+    When I navigate to the "#/active" route
+    Then the todo list shows 2 items
+    And the todo list does not include "Walk the dog"
+    And the "Active" filter link has the "selected" class
+
+  Rule: Completed filter
+
+  Scenario: Completed filter shows only completed todos
+    When I navigate to the "#/completed" route
+    Then the todo list shows 1 item
+    And the todo list shows "Walk the dog"
+    And the "Completed" filter link has the "selected" class
+
+  Rule: Item update in filtered view
+
+  Scenario: Completing an item in the Active filter hides it
+    Given I navigate to the "#/active" route
+    When I click the toggle checkbox on "Buy milk"
+    Then "Buy milk" is not shown in the todo list
+
+  Scenario: Reactivating a completed item in the Completed filter hides it
+    Given I navigate to the "#/completed" route
+    When I click the toggle checkbox on "Walk the dog"
+    Then "Walk the dog" is not shown in the todo list
\ No newline at end of file
diff --git a/features/todos.feature b/features/todos.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..6ad5dd9
